\begin{itemize}
    \item Greta bakes 30 cookies.
    \item Celinda bakes twice as many cookies as Greta.
    \item They eat 10 cookies.
    \item The rest are put in a box.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Solution:}
Greta bakes 30 cookies.
Celinda bakes twice as many cookies as Greta, so she bakes $2 \times 30 = 60$ cookies.
The total number of cookies baked is $30 + 60 = 90$ cookies.
They eat 10 cookies, so the number of cookies remaining is $90 - 10 = 80$ cookies.
The remaining cookies are put in a box, so there are 80 cookies in the box.
\boxed{80}
